WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.700
Before choosing what to log, map the AI workflow.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:17.240
A sovereign AI system may include a user interface, a local model server, a private API, model routing, private RAG retrieval, vector stores, document connectors, tool calls, queues, workers, storage, and output handling.

3
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.700
Each component may need visibility, but not every component needs the same level of detail.

4
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.540
Start with operational questions.

5
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.080
Is the system working?

6
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:32.380
Which model, version, configuration, and workflow handled the request?

7
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.880
Did retrieval use the expected source set?

8
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.420
Did a tool run, and did it require approval?

9
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.400
Did the response fail, time out, or fall back to a degraded path?

10
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.460
Can the team investigate later without exposing sensitive content unnecessarily?

11
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:53.940
User requests and responses are high-risk telemetry areas, so record metadata carefully.

12
00:00:54.040 --> 00:01:05.000
A structured event may capture request type, workflow name, model identifier, status, latency, and error category without storing the full prompt or output.

13
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:11.900
For private RAG, record source decisions and eligibility without copying entire sensitive chunks by default.

14
00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.020
Infrastructure signals matter too.

15
00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:27.880
Monitor model load behavior, queue depth, worker failures, storage pressure, CPU and RAM use, accelerator or GPU pressure where available, disk space, network conditions, and slow dependencies.

16
00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:34.940
A model may appear unreliable when the real issue is an overloaded machine or a stuck document connector.

17
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.500
Good observability follows the workflow end to end.

18
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:47.160
It captures enough to operate, review, and improve the system while keeping telemetry aligned with privacy, ownership, and data boundary expectations.
